# Project

Building a Databricks Medallion Architecture (Bronze -> Silver -> Gold -> Dashboard)
data pipeline for an e-commerce sales use case, as part of a formal AI-capability
assessment. This is an AI-first assessment: prompt history (including rejections and
revisions) is a mandatory deliverable, and the final code must be production-quality —
suitable for a customer-facing or internal design review.

# Stack
Python, PySpark, SQL, Delta Lake, Databricks (Free Edition, serverless-only).

# Data
customers.csv (10,000 rows), orders.csv (100,000 rows), products.csv (500 rows).
Schemas and intentional data quality issues are defined in docs/assessment-requirements.md
— always treat that file as the source of truth for schema and issue counts.

# Hard rules
- Never invent or reference real customer/PII data. All data is synthetic, generated by us.
- Silver layer must NEVER delete bad rows — flag them via a `quality_check_result` column.
- Every function/script needs a docstring/header comment explaining purpose, inputs, outputs.
- Consistent naming: snake_case for Python/SQL identifiers, PascalCase avoided.
- Every non-trivial change should be something I can review and explain — do not silently
  make architectural decisions; ask or flag assumptions instead.
- When asked to implement something, first restate the approach briefly before writing code
  if the task is non-trivial (new file, new layer, schema change).

# Testing
At least one meaningful automated test tier is required: a data-quality assertion test
(proving quality checks catch the seeded issues) and/or a pytest unit test on a
transformation function.

# Documentation debt
Whenever you generate a script, also tell me what should go in its corresponding
ai-prompts/*.md log entry so I don't forget to record it.